│  Final Answer:                                                                                                │
│  **Madrid, Spain: The Ultimate Travel Guide for February 14-16, 2026**                                        │
│  **Traveler Interests: Art, History, Food, Culture**                                                          │
│                                                                                                               │
│  ---                                                                                                          │
│                                                                                                               │
│  ### **Weather Forecast & Packing Tips**                                                                      │
│  Madrid in early February 2026 will feature **cool, dry weather** with daytime highs of **12°C (54°F)** and   │
│  nighttime lows of **2°C (36°F)**. Occasional light rain is possible, so pack:                                │
│  - **Layered clothing**: Thermal base layers, a waterproof jacket, and a scarf.                               │
│  - **Comfortable shoes**: For walking across cobblestone streets and historic sites.                          │
│  - **Warm accessories**: Gloves and a beanie for evenings.                                                    │
│                                                                                                               │
│  ---                                                                                                          │
│                                                                                                               │
│  ### **Key Attractions & Cultural Hotspots**                                                                  │
│  **1. Art & History Must-Visits**                                                                             │
│  - **Prado Museum** (Museo del Prado): Home to **Velázquez’s *Las Meninas***, **Raphael’s *School of          │
│  Athens***, and Spain’s greatest European art collection. **Tip**: Book tickets online to skip lines.         │
│  - **Royal Palace of Madrid**: Explore Baroque opulence, including the **Royal Chapel** and **Tapestries      │
│  Hall**. **Pro Tip**: Visit during the **afternoon** to avoid crowds.                                         │
│  - **Museo Thyssen-Bornemisza**: A stellar mix of Old Masters and modern art (Donatello’s *St. George*,       │
│  Picasso’s *The Weeping Woman*).                                                                              │
│  - **Palacio de la Zarzuela**: A stunning 19th-century palace with royal gardens—book a guided tour for       │
│  insider stories.                                                                                             │
│                                                                                                               │
│  **2. Hidden Gems**                                                                                           │
│  - **Parque del Oeste**: A serene escape with a **Spanish-style garden**, **art installations**, and a        │
│  **miniature train** for kids.                                                                                │
│  - **Casa de las Flores**: A 17th-century flower shop turned art gallery in **Centro Histórico**, with        │
│  hidden courtyards and local crafts.                                                                          │
│  - **Monasterio de San Isidro**: A lesser-known monastery with **Romanesque architecture** and a **daily      │
│  mass** (check opening hours).                                                                                │
│                                                                                                               │
│  ---                                                                                                          │
│                                                                                                               │
│  ### **Food & Drink: Local Flavors**                                                                          │
│  **1. Tapas & Specialties**                                                                                   │
│  - **La Latina**: A neighborhood buzzing with **tapas bars**. Try:                                            │
│    - *Pintxos* (small plates like **jamón ibérico** and **patatas bravas**).                                  │
│    - **Cerveza Artesana** (local craft beers) at **Cervecería 1895**.                                         │
│  - **Mercado de San Miguel**: A vibrant food market with **seafood stalls**, **churros con chocolate**, and   │
│  **artisanal cheeses**. **Tip**: Arrive early for the best selection.                                         │
│  - **Mercado de San Antón**: A quieter market with **organic produce** and **traditional Spanish desserts**   │
│  (like *rosquillas*).                                                                                         │
│                                                                                                               │
│  **2. Michelin-Starred & Cozy Eateries**                                                                      │
│  - **El Celler**: A 3-star restaurant with a focus on **modern Spanish cuisine** (book a table in advance).   │
│  - **Casa Calvo**: A cozy spot for **paella** and **wine pairings** in **Malasaña**.                          │
│                                                                                                               │
│  ---                                                                                                          │
│                                                                                                               │
│  ### **Events & Local Culture**                                                                               │
│  **1. February Festivities**                                                                                  │
│  - **Feria de San Antón (late January–early February)**: Though slightly outside your dates, the **spirit of  │
│  the festival** lingers. Check if any **parades or music events** are scheduled in February.                  │
│  - **Madrid Fashion Week**: If your dates align, this is a **cultural highlight** (look for street art and    │
│  runway shows).                                                                                               │
│                                                                                                               │
│  **2. Local Customs**                                                                                         │
│  - **Dress Code**: Smart casual for museums; **casual** for tapas bars.                                       │
│  - **Etiquette**: **Reserve tables** at restaurants 2–3 days in advance.                                      │
│  - **Public Transport**: Use **metro lines 1, 2, 4, 5, 6, 7, 10** for most attractions. **Trenes de           │
│  Cercanías** (regional trains) connect to **San Sebastián** (for Basque cuisine).                             │
│                                                                                                               │
│  ---                                                                                                          │
│                                                                                                               │
│  ### **Daily Activity Recommendations**                                                                       │
│  **Day 1 (Feb 14): Art & History**                                                                            │
│  - Morning: **Prado Museum** (9:00–13:00).                                                                    │
│  - Afternoon: **Royal Palace** (15:00–18:00).                                                                 │
│  - Evening: Dinner at **Casa Calvo** (19:30) and stroll through **Plaza Mayor**.                              │
│                                                                                                               │
│  **Day 2 (Feb 15): Food & Culture**                                                                           │
│  - Morning: **Mercado de San Miguel** (10:00–14:00) and **tapas tour** in **La Latina**.                      │
│  - Afternoon: **Museo Thyssen-Bornemisza** (15:00–18:00).                                                     │
│  - Evening: **Cervecería 1895** for beer and **churros**.                                                     │
│                                                                                                               │
│  **Day 3 (Feb 16): Hidden Gems & Relaxation**                                                                 │
│  - Morning: **Parque del Oeste** and **Casa de las Flores**.                                                  │
│  - Afternoon: **Monasterio de San Isidro** (15:00–17:00).                                                     │
│  - Evening: Farewell at **El Celler** for a final meal.                                                       │
│                                                                                                               │
│  ---                                                                                                          │
│                                                                                                               │
│  ### **Budget & Costs**                                                                                       │
│  - **Flights**: Book **early February** for **$47–$73** one-way (cheapest on Fridays).                        │
│  - **Accommodation**: Mid-range hotels in **Centro Histórico** cost **$120–$180/night**.                      │
│  - **Food**: **$10–$25** per meal (tapas bars are budget-friendly).                                           │
│  - **Attractions**: **$10–$15** per museum entry (discounts for EU citizens).                                 │
│                                                                                                               │
│  ---                                                                                                          │
│                                                                                                               │
│  ### **Final Tips**                                                                                           │
│  - **Avoid Crowds**: Visit **museums and landmarks** early in the morning.                                    │
│  - **Language**: Learn basic **Spanish phrases** (e.g., *¿Dónde está el baño?*).                              │
│  - **Safety**: Madrid is **safe**, but keep valuables secure in crowded areas.                                │
│                                                                                                               │
│  Madrid’s blend of **art, history, and vibrant culture** makes it the perfect destination for your February   │
│  trip. Enjoy the **cozy charm** of Spanish hospitality and the **rich tapestry** of its heritage! 🇪🇸✨        │
│                                                                                                               │
