│                                                                                                               │
│  ### **Day 1: Art & Royal Heritage**                                                                          │
│  **Morning (9:00–13:00):**                                                                                    │
│  - **Prado Museum** (Museo del Prado)                                                                         │
│    - **Why:** World’s most important collection of European art, including Velázquez’s *Las Meninas* and      │
│  Titian’s *Venus of Urbino*.                                                                                  │
│    - **Tip:** Arrive early to avoid crowds; prioritize highlights like *The Knight, Death, and the Devil*.    │
│                                                                                                               │
│  **Afternoon (15:00–18:00):**                                                                                 │
│  - **Royal Palace of Madrid** (Palacio Real)                                                                  │
│    - **Why:** A 17th-century palace with Baroque architecture, royal apartments, and the **Royal Chapel**.    │
│    - **Tip:** Book tickets in advance; skip the line with a guided tour.                                      │
│                                                                                                               │
│  **Evening (19:30–21:30):**                                                                                   │
│  - **Dinner at Casa Calvo** (Plaza Mayor)                                                                     │
│    - **Why:** A cozy, family-run spot serving *paella* and *tortilla española*.                               │
│    - **Activity:** Stroll through **Plaza Mayor** for shopping and people-watching.                           │
│                                                                                                               │
│  ---                                                                                                          │
│                                                                                                               │
│  ### **Day 2: Culinary & Cultural Exploration**                                                               │
│  **Morning (10:00–14:00):**                                                                                   │
│  - **Mercado de San Miguel**                                                                                  │
│    - **Why:** A vibrant food market with tapas, fresh seafood, and Spanish wines.                             │
│    - **Activity:** Try *croquetas*, *empanadillas*, and *pimientos de Padrón*.                                │
│                                                                                                               │
│  **Afternoon (15:00–18:00):**                                                                                 │
│  - **Museo Thyssen-Bornemisza**                                                                               │
│    - **Why:** A modern art treasure with works by Picasso, Van Gogh, and El Greco.                            │
│    - **Tip:** Use the **free audio guide** to explore Spanish and European masterpieces.                      │
│                                                                                                               │
│  **Evening (19:00–21:00):**                                                                                   │
│  - **Cervecería 1895** (La Latina)                                                                            │
│    - **Why:** A historic beer hall with a lively atmosphere and *churros* (fried pastries).                   │
│    - **Activity:** Join a **tapas walking tour** in La Latina for a taste of local flavors.                   │
│                                                                                                               │
│  ---                                                                                                          │
│                                                                                                               │
│  ### **Day 3: Hidden Gems & Farewell**                                                                        │
│  **Morning (10:00–12:00):**                                                                                   │
│  - **Parque del Oeste**                                                                                       │
│    - **Why:** A peaceful park with a lake, art installations, and a view of the city.                         │
│    - **Activity:** Rent a bike or enjoy a picnic with local cheeses and bread.                                │
│                                                                                                               │
│  **Afternoon (14:00–16:00):**                                                                                 │
│  - **Casa de las Flores** (Casa de Velázquez)                                                                 │
│    - **Why:** A 16th-century mansion turned museum with a garden and art exhibitions.                         │
│    - **Tip:** Explore the **Garden of the Four Seasons** for a tranquil escape.                               │
│                                                                                                               │
│  **Evening (18:00–20:00):**                                                                                   │
│  - **Final Dinner at El Celler** (Barrio de las Letras)                                                       │
│    - **Why:** A Michelin-starred restaurant with a focus on Spanish cuisine and a rooftop view.               │
│    - **Activity:** Sip *txakoli* (Basque wine) and reflect on your trip.                                      │
